**2. `dut_helper.py`** — `AES128DUTHelper`, a plain-Python (non-SV interface) wrapper centralizing all direct `dut` pin access (`dut.start.value`, `dut.key.value`, `dut.ciphertext.value`, …). It fail-fast validates the exact RTL pin list at construction, range-checks 128-bit writes, and exposes grouped helpers (`drive_command`, `sample_outputs`) plus `make_dut_helper(dut)`.

